        "Anandamide is a key endocannabinoid that activates CB1 receptors. It is one of the fatty acid derivatives grouped with 2-arachidonoylglycerol (2-AG). Receptor papers describe 2-AG as a full agonist at CB1 and CB2, while delta-9-THC is characterized as a partial agonist at CB1. Anandamide breakdown is largely the work of fatty acid amide hydrolase (FAAH), the enzyme responsible for that step. Monoacylglycerol lipase (MAGL) is the enzyme usually named for 2-AG breakdown. Those enzymes are not a cultivation practice.",
